      en: "Tio is a small village in the Gash-Barka region of Eritrea, located about 30 km northwest of Barentu. It lies along the Gash River in a savanna landscape. Historically, Tio was a key stop for caravans traveling between the Eritrean highlands and Sudan. The local economy is predominantly pastoral, with cattle, goats, and camels herded by the Tigre people. Some residents practice subsistence farming, growing sorghum and maize. Archaeological surveys have identified stone structures nearby, suggesting ancient habitation. The village has limited infrastructure; it relies on a well for water and has no electricity, though a solar panel powers the health post. Population is estimated at 1,500 to 2,000.",
