      en: "Dghe is a highland village in the Debub region of Eritrea, known for potato farming. It lies at 2,000 meters elevation, with a cool climate. The village has a church and a primary school. Population is around 600. The main crop is potatoes, which are sold in local markets. The area is green and fertile. Dghe is a peaceful agricultural community with traditional lifestyle.",
